# No trailing slash on purpose. `node_modules/` matches a directory only, so a
# node_modules SYMLINK stays untracked-but-visible and a blind `git add -A` stages
# it. Agents working in git worktrees symlink node_modules back to the main
# checkout rather than reinstalling a native better-sqlite3, and two of them hit
# exactly that. Matching both shapes costs nothing.
node_modules
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
# Ledger and fixture data directories. The rule is deliberately unanchored so it catches a `data/`
# anywhere, but that also swallowed `web/src/data/`, which holds the website's JSON-LD source of
# truth. `Layout.astro` imports it, so a fresh clone could not build the site at all: the file had
# never been committed. Re-include that one directory by name. Un-ignoring the DIRECTORY is what
# matters here, because git does not descend into an excluded directory to find a re-included file.
data/
!web/src/data/
# G04's engine lives at `src/core/data/` and the unanchored `data/` rule above swallowed it, exactly
# as it once swallowed `web/src/data/`: the whole engine was authored and then silently un-committed,
# and the branch was pushed unable to compile. Re-include the DIRECTORY by name (git does not descend
# into an excluded directory to find a re-included file, so the directory, not just its files).
!src/core/data/
# ...and G04's engine tests at `test/data/`, swallowed by the same unanchored `data/` rule.
!test/data/
app/.dev-data/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Browser-flow evidence. Reverses D43, which chose to track all of it: at 254 MB across
# 380 files it had become the single largest area in the repo, larger than the engine,
# the Studio and the specs. The runs are reproducible by re-running the flow, so what was
# being preserved was the artifact and not the fact. D46 (29.07.2026).
.claude/ui-tests/runs/
.tmp-support/
.vercel

# Live Nomadik bexio exports (company data, never commit)
# Repo-root owner/company handover exports (bank onboarding, never commit)
.claude/worktrees/

# Orchestrator prompts and per-run planning scratch (scratch, not durable history)

# M00 packaging build outputs (mcpb bundle, macOS app) are artifacts, never committed
packaging/mcpb/build/
packaging/macos/build/
